atlas native-file-digest

architecture native-file-digest
  canonical_name NativeFileDigest
  family external
  domain External / Platform cryptography
  layer external
  semantic_question Can native file receipts use the operating system's digest implementation while preserving exact content identity and read-failure semantics?
  purpose The shared file reader supplies SHA-256 identities to native commands and Fabric. macOS uses CommonCrypto from libSystem; other platforms and BONFYRE_SHA256_PORTABLE builds use the existing portable implementation.
  maturity measured
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/src/bf_sha256.c
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/include/bonfyre.h
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/tests/sha256_file_test.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreHash/tests/file.test.mjs
  internal_calculus one 8 KiB input buffer feeds a private backend context; the exported BfSha256 context and incremental functions retain their portable representation
  invariant identical file bytes produce the same 64-character digest across the system and portable backends; open, stream and close failures publish no digest
  witness lib/libbonfyre/tests/sha256_file_test.c passes eighteen checks on each backend, including partial read failure and descriptor cleanup
  witness cmd/BonfyreHash/tests/file.test.mjs checks both backends against Node crypto across eleven sizes including SHA padding and read-buffer boundaries
  witness packs/no-simulation/native-hash-acceleration-20261013/benchmark.json records five alternating runs at each size; 128 MiB plus 17 bytes improved from median 0.720429 to 0.119173 seconds with equal independent digests on this Mac
  forbidden_inference faster local digest timing -> the same gain on another machine, cold storage, or a complete application workflow
  forbidden_inference a successful digest -> source immutability, file authenticity or effect authority
  known_gap the portable branch is tested on macOS; this change does not claim a Linux execution witness or accelerate the exported incremental in-memory API

interaction hash-uses-native-file-digest
  source cmd-hash
  destination native-file-digest
  relation file_and_duplicate_reads_to_shared_digest
  preserves exact content identity and explicit I/O failure
  drops digest publication on failed reads
  forbidden_inference equal digests -> permission to delete either file
  invalidates_on digest or error contract changing
  witness cmd/BonfyreHash/tests/file.test.mjs
  binding cmd/BonfyreHash/src/main.c

interaction ingest-uses-native-file-digest
  source cmd-ingest
  destination native-file-digest
  relation source_and_normalized_body_to_intake_identity
  preserves source and normalized identities as separate manifest fields
  drops ready manifest creation when either local hash fails
  forbidden_inference both hashes succeeded -> normalization was lossless or the input stayed immutable throughout processing
  invalidates_on hash or intake readiness contract changing
  witness cmd/BonfyreIngest/tests/hash.test.mjs
  binding cmd/BonfyreIngest/src/main.c

interaction compress-uses-native-file-digest
  source cmd-compress
  destination native-file-digest
  relation passport_source_to_generation_digest
  preserves source generation identity across backend choice
  drops a generation digest when the source cannot be read completely
  forbidden_inference a matching generation digest -> authority to replace a physical representation
  invalidates_on passport or digest contract changing
  witness cmd/BonfyreCompress/tests/physical_compiler_test.sh
  binding cmd/BonfyreCompress/src/physical.c

interaction artifacts-use-native-file-digest
  source artifact-graph
  destination native-file-digest
  relation retained_file_to_artifact_identity
  preserves content-addressed artifact identity and read failure
  drops partial-read digests
  forbidden_inference an artifact digest -> evidence that its contents support a claim
  invalidates_on artifact or digest contract changing
  witness engine/core/tests/operator_reference.test.mjs
  binding engine/core/src/fabric.c
